      {
        "id": "pthm-qft-free-fock-statistics",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "CCR/CAR and particle occupations in adopted free models",
        "reference": "research/extended-frameworks-2026-10-03/quantum-field-theory/workers/free-fields/proof-modules.md#FF1",
        "design_state": "Complete conditional CCR/CAR and normalized-mode occupation deduction. It does not prove a general spin-statistics theorem.",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "deps": [
          "post-qft-free-field-model",
          "def-countable-choice",
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces",
          "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "post-qft-free-field-model": "physical-assumption",
          "def-countable-choice": "mathematical-premise",
          "lem-qft-fock-ccr-car": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-qft-fock-and-test-spaces": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "Conditional algebraic consequences of the adopted bosonic scalar symmetric-Fock and Dirac CAR-Fock free models. The result concerns normalizable one-particle wave-packet modes; it is not a general spin-statistics theorem, an interacting-field result, or an empirical claim.",
        "empirical_premises": [],
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "statement": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. In the selected model of\n[[post-qft-free-field-model]], let $H_\\mu$ be the scalar one-particle Hilbert\nspace and let $\\mathcal K=\\mathcal H_+\\oplus\\overline{\\mathcal H_-}$ be the\nDirac particle/antiparticle one-particle space. Let $\\Omega_s$ and $\\Omega_D$\nbe their zero-particle Fock vectors. The assignments of $H_\\mu$ to bosonic\nFock space and $\\mathcal K$ to CAR Fock space are the physical assumptions\nof that postulate.\n\nFor every unit scalar wave-packet mode $h\\in H_\\mu$, define\n$$|n\\rangle_h=\\frac{(a^\\dagger(h))^n}{\\sqrt{n!}}\\Omega_s,\\qquad n\\ge0.$$\nThese vectors are normalized and mutually orthogonal, belong to the\nfinite-particle domain, and\n$$a(h)|n\\rangle_h=\\sqrt n\\,|n-1\\rangle_h,\\qquad a^\\dagger(h)|n\\rangle_h=\\sqrt{n+1}\\,|n+1\\rangle_h,$$\nwhere $a(h)|0\\rangle_h=0$. The maximal operator domains supplied by\n[[lem-qft-fock-ccr-car]] are\n$$D(a(h))=\\left\\{\\Psi=(\\Psi_n)\\in\\mathcal F_s(H_\\mu):\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\|a_n(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\right\\},\\qquad D(a^\\dagger(h))=\\left\\{\\Psi=(\\Psi_n)\\in\\mathcal F_s(H_\\mu):\\sum_{n\\ge0}\\|a_n^\\dagger(h)\\Psi_n\\|^2<\\infty\\right\\}.$$\nDefine the one-mode number operator as the composition\n$$N_h:=a^\\dagger(h)a(h),\\qquad D(N_h):=\\{\\Psi\\in D(a(h)):a(h)\\Psi\\in D(a^\\dagger(h))\\},\\qquad N_h\\Psi:=a^\\dagger(h)(a(h)\\Psi).$$\nThe displayed finite-particle vectors $|n\\rangle_h$ belong to $D(N_h)$ and\nsatisfy $N_h|n\\rangle_h=n|n\\rangle_h$.\n\nFor every unit Dirac particle mode $u\\in\\mathcal H_+$ or antiparticle mode\n$u\\in\\overline{\\mathcal H_-}$, regarded as a vector of $\\mathcal K$, the\nbounded operator $N_u=c^\\dagger(u)c(u)$ is an orthogonal projection. The\none-mode subspace generated by $u$ is the closed span of\n$\\{(c^\\dagger(u))^n\\Omega_D:n\\ge0\\}$. It is spanned by $\\Omega_D$ and\n$c^\\dagger(u)\\Omega_D$; the latter is normalized and\n$c^\\dagger(u)^2=0$. Thus a single Dirac CAR mode has occupation $0$ or $1$.\nAll statements are conditional on the adopted representations and\n$\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. They do not derive which statistics nature assigns to\nall fields and do not assert an experimental observation.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "literature-derived",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 2, §§2.2–2.4, Free Fields, Vacuum, and Particles",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S2.html",
              "locator": "Complete Chapter 2 HTML; oscillator ladder, scalar-field Fock modes, multiparticle states, and number operator."
            },
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted full-text Chapter 5, §§5.2–5.4, Quantizing the Dirac Field",
              "url": "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S5.html",
              "locator": "Complete Chapter 5 HTML; fermionic quantization, vacuum, particle and antiparticle modes."
            },
            {
              "title": "Mark Srednicki, Quantum Field Theory, author-hosted 2006 prepublication book draft",
              "url": "https://www.physics.ucsb.edu/~mark/ms-qft-DRAFT.pdf",
              "locator": "Complete 616-page draft; §3 scalar Fock quantization and §39 fermionic creation/annihilation modes."
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics"
      }
    ]
